+# Level‑4 Governance & Safety Patch — Summary
+
+This patch implements concrete enforcement and operational controls for:
+- Model provenance enforcement (Gatekeeper + admission webhook verifying mcp.provenance annotations and optional Rekor lookups).
+- Image/model supply chain enforcement (deny unsigned/unsourced model deploys).
+- Multi‑model corroboration service (ensemble) that uses conservative aggregation and auto‑requests A2A if verification is low.
+- Continuous verifier calibration workflow (weekly) with optional auto‑patch to `verifier-config` ConfigMap.
+- KMS key rotation helper for S3 objects (AWS) to enable key rotation and re‑encryption.
+- HIL gate service that CD pipelines must call before promoting to production — enforces signed HIL evidence and FMEA linkage.
+- Gatekeeper template to require explicit consent metadata for PII artifacts.
+- Runbook for webhook fail‑open vs fail‑closed decisions.
+
+Operator next steps
+1. Deploy Gatekeeper templates and constraints in audit mode, run for 48–72h, resolve violations, then flip to enforce.
+2. Deploy model_provenance_webhook (HA, TLS) and configure REKOR_URL and FAIL_ON_ERROR as appropriate.
+3. Deploy multi-model ensemble verifier and wire A2A approver URL.
+4. Provide labeled calibration dataset and enable continuous calibration workflow; optionally configure cluster kubeconfig in GitHub secrets for auto-patch.
+5. Run KMS key rotation helper in controlled window and verify re-encryption test objects first.
+6. Integrate HIL gate (call /check) into your CD promotion pipeline OR as an admission check in your promotion workflow.
+7. Ensure consent metadata is attached to PII artifacts and ingestion pipelines call the Presidio adapter from earlier patches.
+
+Acceptance criteria (examples)
+- Deployments in `default` and `aegis-system` without mcp.provenance/signed=true and mcp.provenance/rekor_digest are rejected.
+- Verifier ensemble auto-creates A2A approval requests for low-confidence outputs; human approvals required before sensitive side effects.
+- Weekly calibration run produces a report and threshold is updated in staging configmap automatically (if enabled).
+- KMS rotation script re-encrypts sample objects successfully; secrets updated accordingly.
+- CD promotions fail if HIL evidence or FMEA linkage is missing.
+
